<title>USA: U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. BOXED BEEF CUT-OUT AT 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef sharply lower on moderate demand and heavy offerings.  Select and Choice rib, chuck and round cuts lower, while loin cuts sharply lower. Fresh beef trimmings weak early on moderate demand and offerings with good frozen interest noted. - USDA</p>
<p>------</p>
<p>308 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>105 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>48 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     104.44	104.13	 96.61	 96.06</p>
<p>Changes	  -1.96	 -1.79	 -1.82	 -1.67</p>
<p>Rib	  166.92	165.38	148.37	146.84</p>
<p>Chuck	 72.19	 71.73	 71.20	 69.54</p>
<p>Round	 91.52	 91.52	 87.92	 87.92</p>
<p>Loin	 162.64	162.65	140.43	141.00</p>
<p>Brisket     60.38	 60.38	 60.51	 60.51</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  64.63	 64.55	 64.87	 64.70</p>
<p>Flank	 58.03	 58.03	 57.61	 57.61</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
